  "review_notes": [
    "Platform-user lifecycle is isolated behind /api/v1/platform-users and guarded both at the controller boundary and service capability boundary.",
    "Legacy PLATFORM_AUTHOR remains an explicit compatibility alias while canonical role resolution emits ACADEMIC_STAFF; the legacy tenant-user endpoint no longer resolves academic platform roles.",
    "Role scope is deny-by-default, mixed platform/tenant principals fail closed, platform-user username uniqueness is backed by a partial database index, and soft-deleted platform users are excluded from direct lookup/listing.",
    "Denied capability, self-target, forbidden target, and forbidden role-assignment paths record failure audits without password, token, or credential material.",
    "Live PostgreSQL migration execution, HTTP authorization integration, and browser E2E remain deferred validation boundaries for the later integration phase."
